[03/10/26]	rasmol.c
		Fixed main()'s interactive command loop spinning at 100% CPU
		forever once stdin reaches EOF without an "exit"/"quit" ever
		being issued (e.g. a piped/automated session, or closing the
		terminal with Ctrl-D) - ReadCharacter()'s EOF (-1) was never
		checked, so FetchCharacter()/getc(stdin) kept returning EOF
		millions of times a second with nothing to stop the loop.
		Compounding this, the loop variable "ch" was declared char,
		which is unsigned on this aarch64 target, so EOF (-1) got
		silently truncated to 255 before any check could even see it
		- widened it to int and added a "ch==EOF -> break" check,
		which reaches the same RasMolExit() a "quit" command does.
		This is independent of -script: LoadScriptFile() (command.c)
		reads script files through its own getc(fp) loop, so sourcing
		a script of predefined selections/styles and then continuing
		interactively (-script setup.rsc, no quit at the end of the
		script) is unaffected; only the real stdin stream's own EOF
		is now handled.

[03/10/26]	rasmol.c
		Fixed a double-free that aborted RasMol (SIGABRT, glibc
		"double free detected in tcache") at the end of almost any
		-script run. main()'s own fclose(fp) right after calling
		LoadScriptFile(fp,...) was closing a FILE* that
		LoadScriptFile() (command.c) already closes itself on every
		return path (end of script, "exit" command, or process exit
		via "quit"/RasMolExit()), so the handle's heap buffer got
		freed twice. Confirmed fixed, and the rest of the run is
		clean, under valgrind --error-exitcode. Spotted this while
		investigating what looked like mmCIF reader crashes, but the
		bug is unrelated to parsing and just as reproducible loading
		a plain PDB file via -script.

[03/10/26]	rasmol.c command.c infile.c transfor.h
		Cleaned up every warning the modern gcc/SDL2 build was
		producing (make now builds silent). Added the missing
		SetTraceTemperature() prototype to transfor.h (was an
		implicit-int declaration in command.c); added a top level
		<string.h> include to rasmol.c (strcmp etc. were implicitly
		declared outside the VMS build); fixed select()'s unused
		fd_set* arguments casting to a nonexistent "struct fd_set"
		type instead of the real fd_set typedef; added braces round
		an if/for/if-else chain in infile.c's ProcessFeatures() that
		gcc flagged as a dangling-else trap; gave SavePDBMolecule's
		"ch" TER-record variable an initial value to resolve a
		maybe-uninitialized warning (prev/ch are always set together,
		so this was a flow-analysis false positive, not a real bug);
		replaced the strncpy() calls added for the mmCIF loop-row
		reader with a small memcpy based helper, since GCC's
		stringop-truncation check can't see the explicit NUL write
		that already followed; and reworked InitHelpFile's priming
		fgets() so its result is actually inspected, since glibc's
		fortified fgets is marked warn_unused_result in a way a bare
		(void) cast does not silence.

[03/10/26]	infile.c infile.h command.c command.h rasmol.c
		Added a dependency-free mmCIF reader (LoadCIFMolecule, in
		infile.c), since RasMol previously only knew how to write
		CIF (SaveCIFMolecule) and not read it. Implements a small
		tag/loop tokeniser for the subset of the mmCIF grammar the
		PDB/AlphaFold actually emit ('#' comments, quoted strings,
		';' multi-line text fields) and structurally parses the
		"_atom_site" loop by column name rather than fixed column
		position, since mmCIF is tag/loop based, not column based
		like PDB. Atom/element typing is built to match the same
		4-column convention ComplexAtomType()/GetElemNumber() use
		for PDB files (justified by the explicit type_symbol rather
		than guessed from column position), so CIF-loaded structures
		get the same backbone tracing, cartoons and element colouring
		as PDB ones. A few summary fields (_entry.id, _struct.title,
		_cell.*, _symmetry.*) are also read to populate the same
		fields HEADER/COMPND/CRYST1 fill in for PDB. Hooked up via
		the existing (previously write-only) FormatCIF plumbing in
		command.c's FetchFile.
		Also added GuessMoleculeFormat() (command.c/command.h),
		since without it a bare "load foo.cif" or "rasmol foo.cif"
		silently defaulted to the fixed-column PDB parser, which
		misreads free-form CIF text as 80-column fields and produces
		garbage, visually flattened coordinates. Format is now
		guessed from the .cif/.mmcif extension whenever the user
		doesn't say otherwise, in both the "load" command and the
		command-line filename argument; explicit "-cif"/"load cif"
		are unaffected. Added "-cif" to the -help usage line.

[03/10/26]	sdlwin.c rasmol.h rasmol.c Makefile Makefile.in
		Replaced the X11/Xlib display backend (x11win.c) with a new
		SDL2 backend (sdlwin.c), so RasMol no longer needs an X
		server (ie. XQuartz on macOS) to run. x11win.c drew its own
		menu bar, scrollbars and dials-box by hand with raw Xlib
		calls on top of blitting the renderer's framebuffer; the
		menu/scrollbar/dials-box chrome has been dropped in favour
		of RasMol's existing command language, but mouse-driven
		rotate/translate/zoom/slab, click-to-pick and window resize
		all still work and were ported across unchanged in spirit.
		Also fixed Card/Long/Pixel (rasmol.h) to be pinned to 32 bits
		via _LONGLONG, since plain "long" is 64 bits on modern LP64
		systems and was silently corrupting the pixel-packing code;
		switched on THIRTYTWOBIT (24-bit true colour) as the default
		since 256-colour displays are now obsolete. Tightened the
		stdin/event poll in rasmol.c from 1s to 20ms while a display
		window is open, for responsive dragging. Makefile/Makefile.in
		now build against SDL2 (via sdl2-config) instead of hardcoded
		per-workstation X11 flags from 1995.

[09/04/96]	script.c
		Modified the generation of script files to fix a bug in
		writing the "colour axes" command to include commas. Special
		to Guy Slater.

[29/03/96]	script.c
		Modified the generation of script files to avoid writing
		"colour ribbons none" at each residue, which is the default.
		Thanks to Alan Lewis.

[21/11/95]	command.c
		Changed the conditions in FetchFile on when RasMol determines
		bonds itself to the condition "bonds < atoms-chains".  This
                allows multiple connected fragments.  Thanks to William Hart.

[10/11/95]	infile.c x11win.c
		Made several #ifdef VMS changes to allow RasMol to compile
                with VAX C.  Thanks to Gail Schuman.

[10/11/95]	pixutils.h pixutils.c repres.c
		Changed the field names hx, hy and hz in structure Knot to
                to dx, dy and dz to avoid clash with predefined AIX macro hz.
                Thanks to Hiroki Morizono.

[09/11/95]	transfor.c
		Fixed bug in ApplyTransform() that caused RasMol to crash if
		all atoms have the same co-ordinates. Thanks to Guy Slater.

[06/11/95]	script.c
		Fixed bug in RasMol script generation that outputs the
		background colour before the zap command (which resets
		the background colour to black). Thanks to Niels Kristian 
                Bech Jensen.

[20/10/95]      infile.c
		Fixed bug in RasMol CHARMm file format reader.  RasMol now
                uses the standard PDB residue numbering in column 56, rather
                than the sequential numbering in column 5.  Thanks to Milan
                Hodoscek

